From: EngineOS maintainers
Subject: Unlink the server socket when shutdown begins

Once SIGTERM has initiated server shutdown, new clients must not connect to the
dying server. Unlinking the pathname immediately lets a following tmux command
create a new server instead of connecting successfully and then receiving
"server exited unexpectedly". Existing clients and the listening descriptor
remain valid until normal shutdown completes.

This also makes upstream regress/command-order.sh deterministic when it starts
a second server immediately after kill-server.

diff --git a/server.c b/server.c
index a326c75e..13621234 100644
--- a/server.c
+++ b/server.c
@@ -436,6 +436,9 @@ server_signal(int sig)
 	switch (sig) {
 	case SIGINT:
 	case SIGTERM:
+		/* Stop new clients reaching a server which is already exiting. */
+		if (server_fd != -1)
+			unlink(socket_path);
 		server_exit = 1;
 		server_send_exit();
 		break;
